---
/**
 * Privacy policy for the pre-launch site.
 *
 * Written against what this site ACTUALLY does — one email field, an optional
 * city, session-scoped attribution, and analytics that are currently not even
 * configured. Every claim below was checked against the code rather than copied
 * from a template: see src/pages/api/waitlist.ts, src/scripts/forms.ts and the
 * UTM/consent scripts in src/layouts/Base.astro.
 *
 * If any of those change — an analytics key gets set, a CRM is wired to
 * WAITLIST_WEBHOOK_URL — this document has to change in the same commit.
 */
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { PLACE } from '../lib/claims';

const VERSION = 'v1.0';
const EFFECTIVE = '17 September 2026';
---
<Doc
  title="Privacy Policy | Halal Goes"
  description="What Halal Goes collects from this pre-launch website, why, how long we keep it, and how to get it removed. Ontario, Canada."
  heading="Privacy policy."
  standfirst="One email address, an optional city, and nothing we can identify you by beyond that. Here is exactly what happens to it."
  version={VERSION}
  effective={EFFECTIVE}
>
  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">01</span>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We collect your email address, and only if you type it in.</li>
      <li>We use it to email you when we open, and afterwards only about newly verified kitchens near you.</li>
      <li>We do not sell it, rent it, or pass it to restaurants or anyone else for their own marketing.</li>
      <li>You can have it deleted at any time, and you don't have to give a reason.</li>
      <li>There are no advertising or tracking cookies on this site.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The rest of this page is the detail behind those five lines.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">02</span>What we collect</h2>
    <h3>Your email address</h3>
    <p>
      Collected only when you submit the waitlist form. Restaurant owners submit a work email on
      the same basis.
    </p>
    <h3>A city or area, if you choose to add one</h3>
    <p>
      After you join, we offer one optional field asking where in {PLACE.province} you are. It is
      optional in the real sense — skipping it changes nothing about what you receive. We use it to
      decide where to open first.
    </p>
    <h3>How you arrived</h3>
    <p>
      If you reach the site from a campaign link, we read the <code>utm_*</code> parameters and the
      referring page and keep them in your browser's session storage, so that if you sign up we
      know which channel worked. It is cleared when you close the tab, and it contains no
      information about you.
    </p>
    <h3>Ordinary server logs</h3>
    <p>
      Our host records requests, including IP addresses, as part of running and securing the site.
      We don't use those logs to build a profile of you.
    </p>
    <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
    <p>
      No name, no phone number, no address, no payment details, no account. We do not ask for a
      phone number, and if one is ever submitted to our waitlist endpoint it is discarded rather
      than stored.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">03</span>Your consent, and the record of it</h2>
    <p>
      Canada's anti-spam legislation requires your express consent before we send you commercial
      email. You give that by entering your address and submitting the form, underneath a notice
      saying what we will send.
    </p>
    <p>
      We store <strong>the exact sentence you were shown</strong>, the date and time, how the
      consent was given, and which part of the page you were on — so that if the wording on the
      site ever changes, the record still shows what you actually agreed to. If we cannot record
      all of that, we refuse the submission rather than keep your address.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">04</span>Analytics and cookies</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>This site currently runs no analytics at all</strong> and sets no cookies. If we
      enable privacy-friendly analytics later, a banner will ask you first and nothing will load
      until you say yes — declining is remembered and is not re-asked on every visit.
    </p>
    <p>
      The only browser storage we use today is the session-scoped attribution described above, and
      it is discarded when you close the tab.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">05</span>Who else touches it</h2>
    <p>
      Our website and its form endpoint are hosted by Vercel, which processes requests on our
      behalf. When we connect an email tool to send the launch announcement, it will process your
      address on our behalf too, under contract and for no other purpose.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell or rent personal information, and we do not pass your address to restaurants.
      Data may be stored or processed outside {PLACE.country}, which means it can be subject to the
      laws of the country it is held in.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">06</span>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it, or until we decide not to launch — at which
      point we tell the list and then delete it. We keep the consent record itself for as long as
      the law requires us to be able to prove consent, and no longer.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">07</span>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under Canadian privacy law you can ask us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Tell you what we hold about you, and give you a copy.</li>
      <li>Correct it if it is wrong.</li>
      <li>Delete it.</li>
      <li>Stop emailing you — which you can also do yourself from any email we send.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We will not make you explain why, and asking costs you nothing. If you are unhappy with how
      we handle a request, you can complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">08</span>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served over HTTPS, the form endpoint re-validates everything before it stores
      anything, and access to the list is limited to the people who need it. No system is perfect,
      and we would rather say that than claim otherwise.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">09</span>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the version and date at the top change with it. If a change affects
      what we do with an address we already hold, we will email the list rather than quietly edit
      this page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">10</span>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions and deletion requests go to the address below. It is not published yet —
      we are showing you the empty field rather than an address nobody is reading. Until it is
      live, replying to any email we send you reaches us.
    </p>
    <div class="doc doc-gap">
      <p class="mono" style="margin:0 0 10px">Privacy contact</p>
      <p style="margin:0"><span class="doc-blank" aria-label="not yet published"></span></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Doc>
